<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon kill 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a11261db3b31e3a35d4fcb1c23047d0d69c1f4c129610d1aaf29932e10ecb1c6</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:10:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-israeli-strikes-on-southern-lebanon-kill-11" /><summary type="html">Israeli strikes ⁠on a ​southern Lebanese town early on Monday killed at least 11 people including two children ​and two medics, Lebanon's state news agency said. Israel has intensified its bombardment of south Lebanon in recent days despite a June ceasefire that was meant ​to halt fighting ‌between the Israeli military and Lebanese armed ⁠group Hezbollah.</summary></entry><entry><title>Céline Dion and Jay-Z bring their hits to Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fadcd08076747c64409c6d936d0cb2c22f7dec4a870967242d560ae776ae4c2f</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:05:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260907-c%C3%A9line-dion-and-jay-z-bring-their-hits-to-paris" /><summary type="html">In this edition of our arts24 music show, Jennifer Ben Brahim brings us a roundup of some of the week's most anticipated Paris concerts. From Céline Dion kicking off her 16 sold-out shows at La Défense Arena, to American rapper Jay-Z celebrating his 30-year career at the Stade de France, we've got you covered.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>What now for Germany's Merz after AfD win?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02d34ca22360dbdf5df565cf52521b30d221d3e8ac731a9669d074c78e81aa50</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:01:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-what-now-for-germany-s-merz-after-afd-win" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD's triumph in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt marks a defeat for German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and sends a warning to other European leaders battling the same mixture of slow growth and disillusion with mainstream politics. In an increasingly polarized political system, Merz, whose personal approval ratings have sunk ‌to record lows, was one of the main targets of voter ire over the cost of living, pensions and economic insecurity. France 24’s Philip Turle takes a look at what the AfD’s victory means for the German leader and for Europe.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt poll: 'A huge blow for the CDU, but also a huge win for the AfD'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9149316332c312d44b51c4bbe8a15750b9fb89a0169ea98cd457e4215ebc5298</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1" /><summary type="html">Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Markus Ziener, Visiting Senior Fellow at the German Marshall Fund. He interprets the AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt as a potentially historic turning point in post-war German politics. For Ziener, the significance lies not only in the scale of the far right’s electoral success, but also in the constituency behind it: many AfD voters, he argues, were previously politically disengaged rather than simply defecting from established parties. This complicates conventional explanations of the result as a straightforward transfer of support from the CDU to the AfD and raises a deeper question about the political expectations of a newly mobilised electorate.</summary></entry><entry><title>How far-right AfD breakthrough may ‘cause absolute chaos’ in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:759e297d5a2ed37b9a9ba29c59a3b2208a3424598b7a54d76cc4322d1c8f2864</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:45:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd" /><summary type="html">Germany’s Alternative for Germany (AfD) came out well ahead in Sunday’s regional elections in the state of Saxony-Anhalt, becoming the first far-right party to come close to gaining power at the regional level since World War II. The lead candidate of the party in the state, Ulrich Siegmund, said Monday that his party had already initiated talks towards building a governing majority.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Two children among dead in Israeli strikes on Lebanon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e40e214870ea6c1aeb3569ec759f33328bbd657861036063d97fd4e676394bff</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:20:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-two-children-among-dead-in-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon" /><summary type="html">Israeli airstrikes overnight killed 11 people in a south Lebanon village, including two infants, Lebanese state media said Monday, a day after separate raids left seven dead. France 24's Renée Davis in Beirut has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: 'Shocked' Merz speaks after far-right election victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf3c413953b3b95effac0b2691b77fa0889c3b980a57d469eff706d8efe154e5</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:04:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-replay-shocked-merz-speaks-after-far-right-election-victory" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said Monday he was "deeply shocked" after his centre-right party suffered a heavy loss in a state poll to the far-right AfD, but vowed to push on with reforms. Watch his press conference in full above.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Idiots and traitors’: World reacts to AfD’s election victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9b2878dc62f8d634272629f7fe7147c5a926896558bae97d9826a92796edeac</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:02:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-idiots-and-traitors-world-reacts-to-afd-s-election-victory" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany (AfD) surged into first place in state elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday. The result puts a far-right party within reach of power at the state level for the first time in the country since World War II. The outcome has European capitals taking notice, particularly in France where the campaign for next year's presidential elections has gotten underway.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN rapporteur says Israeli rubble-clearing in Gaza could erase 'atrocity crimes' evidence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:805f57e7cba322a09492a4a00abe69048ef79f0f75a0ec941cea2312fb41623c</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:51:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-un-rapporteur-says-israeli-rubble-clearing-in-gaza-could-erase-atrocity-crimes-evidence" /><summary type="html">The United Nations special rapporteur on Palestinian territories Francesca Albanese warned Monday that large-scale rubble removal in parts of Gaza under Israeli control could risk erasing "evidence relevant to the investigation of alleged international crimes". Israel's bombardment and ground offensive on Gaza has killed more than 73,000 Palestinians, according to Gaza's health ministry.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'We’re all in crisis': Populist far-right 'trend' sweeping across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a57a49433a19963edd2489d25aaf2fefd8d4f102433b01f3b6b093c89933d729</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome our international affairs editor, Philip Turle, and Sylvie Bermann, France's first female ambassador to three member countries of the United Nations Security Council: China, the United Kingdom and Russia. The AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt should be understood, according to Sylvie Bermann, as part of a wider transformation of European politics rather than as an isolated German electoral shock. Brexit and Donald Trump’s victories helped normalise political positions previously regarded as outside the governing mainstream, while successive economic and geopolitical crises have weakened confidence in established parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>Driverless taxi services are rolling out fast across the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb521e4d1918f0555674ae70af9291538471c6b31a77becbd3e2049cb5929b6c</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:29:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20260907-driverless-taxi-services-are-rolling-out-fast-across-the-world" /><summary type="html">From Austin to London, the current robotaxi boom is raising hard questions about safety and jobs. We take a closer look in this edition of Tech 24.</summary><category term="Tech 24" /></entry><entry><title>Who could form a coalition with Germany's AfD after election victory?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:042bf8a88cab2d2cbf4309239136841dd512df9622347f2a3d9e943212e628fc</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:23:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-who-could-form-a-coalition-with-germany-s-afd-after-election-victory" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD won a landslide victory in a key regional election Sunday in the ex-communist east, a result seen as a stinging rebuke for Chancellor Friedrich Merz, but looked set to miss out on an absolute majority to govern alone. The big question now is who, if anyone, will be willing to form a coalition with the party, says France 24's correspondent Nick Holdsworth.</summary></entry><entry><title>French wine yields drop to new historic low after searing summer heat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8518fdbbe637f3b2437374783a9cc4c2648d57477db78f4fe2fdda8b7b42475</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T11:57:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260907-scorching-summer-pushes-french-wine-harvest-to-new-historic-low" /><summary type="html">French wine production is expected to suffer its worst harvest in some 70 years with the agriculture ministry on Monday forecasting a 6 percent drop in output after a summer of scorching temperatures, heatwaves and drought. France last week announced more than €1 billion in emergency support for farmers.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Five dead after Amazon cargo plane overshoots runway in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:734c375a47e6aa9792f5d1ad3959bf0438b9b3741a38a05444389b0298626b8e</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:54:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-five-dead-after-amazon-cargo-plane-overshoots-runway-in-miami" /><summary type="html">At least five people died when an Amazon Prime Air cargo flight overran a runway and crashed while landing at Miami International ​Airport on Sunday, local ‌officials said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lebanon president calls for US help after deadly Israeli strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e990234abc67e5de29720ed92df7860d7950458c52ba62268b2ee161e341afd</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:21:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-lebanon-president-calls-for-us-help-after-deadly-israeli-strikes" /><summary type="html">Lebanese President Joseph Aoun has urged Washington and the international community to help stop Israeli attacks, with strikes on the south of the country killing at least 11 people on Sunday despite a truce and a framework deal aimed at halting the violence.</summary></entry><entry><title>Segregated schools and citizen ‘watch groups’: the AfD’s plans for Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba92c9de251987e8fbfa389b3f02e9f3cfb2e35740ffdf23a6c752915f2bc5e8</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:13:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-segregated-schools-and-citizen-watch-groups-the-afd-s-plans-for-saxony-anhalt" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany (AfD) surged into first place in state elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday, exit polls showed, putting a far-right party within reach of power at the state level for the first time since World War Two. So who are the AfD, and what could it mean for voters in the state? Rachael Griffiths has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Jubilation and pain': German far right marches to victory in key state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2da7cc5ad102ba5f72454e7805d360fbe692c0df8a2a7654c553873743215100</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:05:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260907-jubilation-and-pain-german-far-right-marches-to-victory-in-key-state-election" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, September 7: The far right marches to victory in a German state election: what does this mean for the future of Germany and Europe at large? Also: the Daily Telegraph publishes an exclusive interview with the sons of former Pakistani PM Imran Khan about his imprisonment conditions in Pakistan. Plus the US Open descends into chaos after influencers, weed and disruptions stir controversy.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Jamaica’s legal approach: Were forced transportation &amp; African enslavement lawful under English law?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60eea918c20846e41777e382b078396d46fafa45161eedbbb87883e4b002ab3c</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T10:03:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-jamaica-s-legal-approach-were-forced-transportation-african-enslavement-lawful-under-english-law" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Jamaica’s Minister of Culture, Gender, Entertainment and Sport, Olivia Grange. According to Grange, the country’s reparations initiative attempts to shift the debate over British slavery from the terrain of political discretion to that of legal accountability. Was the capture, transportation and chattel enslavement of Africans in Jamaica ever lawful? Jamaica’s petition therefore asks King Charles III, in his capacity as King of Jamaica, to refer three questions to the Privy Council concerning English law, international law and Britain’s possible obligation to provide a reparatory remedy.</summary></entry><entry><title>Far-right AfD wins crushing victory in German state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eaf5b1e385d9534555c102000d44ba9377d81a845ac062195c3048431171af2e</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:55:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-far-right-afd-wins-crushing-victory-in-german-state-election" /><summary type="html">The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) surged into first place in state elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday, exit polls showed, putting it within reach of power at the state level for the first time since World War Two, though falling just short of an overall majority.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why are tourists flocking to French pharmacies?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84c0609858326e74d716a7c7edc86488d17ee7f181517cc728dbebd2da0dfee9</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:44:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-why-are-tourists-flocking-to-french-pharmacies" /><summary type="html">After visiting the monuments and department stores, for some tourists in France, it’s off to the pharmacy. More and more foreign tourists are taking advantage of their stay to stock up on cosmetic products, sold in many pharmacies in France, which are known to be less expensive and very popular on social media.</summary></entry><entry><title>German startup carries out Europe's first commercial space launch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e531db7c5adc970a4a7a2a6c55a1973099281de70e87e60dc7a1570a17e85b3d</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:41:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-german-startup-carries-out-europe-s-first-commercial-space-launch" /><summary type="html">German startup Isar Aerospace successfully launched its Spectrum rocket into orbit from Norway on Saturday night, marking the first ever such launch by a commercial entity from European soil. European firms are racing to make up ground in the lucrative launch industry, currently dominated by America's SpaceX.</summary></entry><entry><title>German startup notches Europe's first successful private orbital launch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1512791952ba9def648b1831669d3d2066a1fea41fe5860e78223f802a52a056</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:32:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260907-german-startup-notches-europe-s-first-successful-private-orbital-launch" /><summary type="html">German startup Isar Aerospace becomes the first company to achieve a successful private orbital space launch. But first: Germany's far-right AfD party scores a big electoral victory, pushed along in part by the country's structural economic crisis and its fiscal policies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal holds a day of mourning as rescuers continue search for flood missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fbd9d6a5992a57fb1bfbe55939e0aa3e2719a9e7c8bcec0be87fbbd71cd8229</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:25:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-nepal-holds-a-day-of-mourning-as-rescuers-continue-search-for-flood-missing" /><summary type="html">Grief-stricken Nepalis entered the traditional Hindu last day of mourning on Monday for the hundreds who died in the catastrophic flood along the country's border with China even as the government kept search operations going ​after four ‌miracle rescues in recent days.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany seeks to dismiss Nicaragua's Gaza genocide case at top UN court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f214068980cbe6f7cec1cff5089619658b41851efecfb4195a49972b33f0ee34</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:14:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-germany-seeks-dismissal-of-nicaragua-s-gaza-genocide-case-at-top-un-court" /><summary type="html">Germany is set to ask the International Court of Justice on Monday to dismiss a case accusing Berlin of "facilitating genocide" in Gaza by supporting Israel after the deadly October 7, 2023 attacks by Hamas militants. The details of the case, filed by Nicaragua in 2024, have not yet been made public.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
